+// A refspec argument the guard cannot statically prove safe: an unresolved shell variable
+// ($FOO/${FOO}/$(...)) or backtick command-substitution — the guard only ever sees the LITERAL
+// argv text, but the worker's own shell expands these before git ever runs (#679 gate② P1(a):
+// `git push origin HEAD:$SAPWOOD_DEFAULT_BRANCH` expands to `HEAD:main` at runtime even though
+// the token equals neither "main" nor anything the exact-match check below recognizes) — or a
+// `*` wildcard destination, which can match the default branch's ref without ever naming it
+// (#679 gate② P1(c): `refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*`).
